[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Security Best Practices in React Native: SSL Pinning, Secure Storage, and Code Obfuscation"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Building secure mobile applications requires a multi-layered defense strategy. By default, React Native apps are vulnerable to Man-in-the-Middle (MITM) attacks, data extraction from local storage, and reverse engineering. This tutorial covers three critical hardening techniques: SSL Pinning, Secure Storage, and Code Obfuscation."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Implementing SSL Pinning"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"SSL pinning prevents MITM attacks by validating the server's SSL certificate against a known copy stored within the app, rather than trusting the OS certificate store blindly. Because React Native's built-in fetch relies on platform networking APIs, native modules or specialized libraries are required."},{"order":5,"type":"paragraph","text":"Using a community-tested library like react-native-ssl-public-key-pinning or writing a custom native module is standard practice. Below is an example configuration using a popular networking library setup:"},{"order":6,"type":"code","text":"import {initializeSslPinning} from 'react-native-ssl-public-key-pinning';

const configurePinning = async () => {
  try {
    await initializeSslPinning({
      'yourdomain.com': {
        includeSubdomains: true,
        publicKeyHashes: [
          'Base64EncodedPublicKeyHash1==',
          'Base64EncodedPublicKeyHash2=='
        ],
      },
    });
    console.log('SSL Pinning initialized successfully');
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Failed to initialize SSL pinning', error);
  }
};"},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Secure Storage (Keychain and Keystore)"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Never store sensitive data like authentication tokens, passwords, or personal identifiable information (PII) in AsyncStorage. AsyncStorage is unencrypted and easily accessible on rooted or jailbroken devices. Instead, use platform-specific secure storage: iOS Keychain and Android Keystore."},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"The library react-native-encrypted-storage provides a secure wrapper around these native mechanisms. Here is how to securely store and retrieve a user session token:"},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"import EncryptedStorage from 'react-native-encrypted-storage';

async function storeUserSession(token) {
  try {
    await EncryptedStorage.setItem('user_session', JSON.stringify({token}));
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error saving secure data', error);
  }
}

async function getUserSession() {
  try {
    const session = await EncryptedStorage.getItem('user_session');
    if (session) {
      return JSON.parse(session);
    }
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error retrieving secure data', error);
  }
  return null;
}"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Code Obfuscation"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"JavaScript bundles in React Native can be easily extracted and reverse-engineered because they are plain text zipped inside the application asset folder. Code obfuscation makes it significantly harder for attackers to read business logic, API endpoints, and hardcoded keys."},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"For Android, you should enable ProGuard or R8 in your android/gradle.properties file. Set the following flags to shrink and obfuscate your release builds:"},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"android.enableProguard=true
android.enableR8=true"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Additionally, you can integrate tools like javascript-obfuscator into your Metro bundler or build pipeline to rename variables, mangle strings, and add dead code. Here are the key security practices to remember:"},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always pin certificates or public keys to protect against intercepting proxies like Charles or Burp Suite."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Never use AsyncStorage for sensitive tokens or cryptographic keys."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Enable ProGuard/R8 for Android and configure dead-code elimination and string encryption for iOS."}]
